{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795221,"nonce":"s5o6Pu4Z2Fk9f++l6dyTpYMmkFA=","title":"Build Start/Join Jam, invitations, presence and follow-mode UI","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P1\n\nScope\nAdd command-center and UI entry points for start/join/leave/end, room overview, sharing selection, invitation roles/revocation, connection state, participant list, team chat and opt-in follow mode. Bind each room to its specific project/window and personal/team owner; restore safe metadata rather than auto-sharing a restored workspace. Clearly distinguish connection, sync, save and host/payer states. Separate team activity and audience chat. Closing/hiding a panel does not accidentally terminate an intended call or retain presentation resources.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nNative UI fixtures demonstrate two windows in different teams without cross-activation or cross-billing. Keyboard navigation, long names, small windows, both themes, reconnect/cancel/failure states and explicit sharing are covered. Leave/end closes intended room work and clears only its own presentation. Ordinary editing and Welcome remain usable without sign-in.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}